# Copy this file to .dev.vars (gitignored) for local `wrangler pages dev`
# runs. Nothing here is a secret — these are test-only seams that make local
# dev tolerable, and production never sets any of them (see the comment at
# each seam's call site in the source file named).

# Lets tests/auth-endpoints.test.mjs (and manual poking at the local app) be
# re-run against the same long-lived dev server without tripping the
# register/login flood brakes. Local dev never sends CF-Connecting-IP, so
# every caller shares one "unknown" bucket per brake — without this, a
# second or third consecutive run fails on a 429 that has nothing to do with
# the change you're testing. The seam gates BOTH brake layers — the durable
# one (the LIMITER Durable Object's /brake counter) persists in .wrangler
# state across dev-server restarts, so without this even a restart wouldn't
# clear a tripped brake. See functions/api/auth/register.js and
# functions/api/auth/login.js for the check, and
# tests/auth-endpoints.unit.test.mjs's "does not appear in wrangler.toml"
# test for the guarantee that this can never reach production by accident.
AUTH_TEST_BYPASS_RATE_LIMIT=1

# Needed only for tests/generate.test.mjs / tests/generate.unit.test.mjs
# (Instant mode). Makes the endpoint return a canned envelope instead of
# calling OpenRouter — gate/quota/validation logic is fully exercised with
# zero spend. See functions/api/generate.ts.
# OPENROUTER_PROXY_KEY=dev-placeholder
# INSTANT_TEST_ECHO=1
